-- title:
--   Unitary intertwiners out of a signed polynomial carrier also intertwine Hermitian tensor powers
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a natural number, let $S_q=\{1,\dots,q\}\times\{0,1\}$ be the signed spin alphabet (sector $0$ is the even sector, sector $1$ the odd sector), and let $G=U(q)\times U(q)$.
--
--   For a Young diagram $\lambda$ with at most $q$ rows, its *polynomial carrier* $V_\lambda$ is the following subspace of $(\mathbb{C}^q)^{\otimes\lambda}$, the tensor power whose factors are indexed by the cells of $\lambda$. Let $h_\lambda=\sum_{\sigma}\operatorname{sgn}(\sigma)\,\sigma\cdot e_{\mathrm{row}}$, where $e_{\mathrm{row}}$ is the basis tensor that gives each cell the colour of its row and $\sigma$ runs over the permutations of the cells preserving every column (acting by permuting tensor factors). Then $V_\lambda=\operatorname{span}\{g^{\otimes\lambda}h_\lambda: g\in U(q)\}$, the irreducible polynomial representation of $U(q)$ generated by this highest-weight vector. For every Hermitian $A\in\mathbb{C}^{q\times q}$ the operator $A^{\otimes\lambda}$ maps $V_\lambda$ into itself; let $\pi_\lambda(A)$ denote its restriction to $V_\lambda$.
--
--   Fix Young diagrams $a,b$ with at most $q$ rows. The *signed carrier* $V_{a,b}=V_a\otimes V_b$ is a representation of $G$ via $(g_0,g_1)\mapsto\pi_a(g_0)\otimes\pi_b(g_1)$. For a finite set $\tau$, the *signed tensor space* $X_\tau=(\mathbb{C}^{S_q})^{\otimes\tau}$ is a representation of $G$ via $(g_0,g_1)\mapsto(g_0\oplus g_1)^{\otimes\tau}$, where $g_0\oplus g_1$ is the block-diagonal matrix acting by $g_0$ on the even sector and by $g_1$ on the odd sector of $\mathbb{C}^{S_q}$.
--
--   **Theorem.** Let $L:V_{a,b}\to X_\tau$ be a $G$-intertwiner, that is, a complex-linear map with $L\circ\big(\pi_a(g_0)\otimes\pi_b(g_1)\big)=(g_0\oplus g_1)^{\otimes\tau}\circ L$ for all $(g_0,g_1)\in G$. Then for all Hermitian matrices $A_0,A_1\in\mathbb{C}^{q\times q}$ and all $v\in V_{a,b}$,
--   $$
--   L\Big(\big(\pi_a(A_0)\otimes\pi_b(A_1)\big)v\Big)=(A_0\oplus A_1)^{\otimes\tau}\,L v .
--   $$
--
--   Thus equivariance under the compact group $G$ upgrades automatically to equivariance under pairs of Hermitian matrices acting through tensor powers. In particular a product operator $\rho^{\otimes\tau}$ with $\rho=A_0\oplus A_1$ block diagonal, such as a density matrix preserving both sectors, can be moved through every intertwiner; this is what allows one to twirl product states onto isotypic components of $X_\tau$ and to bound their norms there.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $L$ is a `Representation.IntertwiningMap` from `SignedCarrier.rep a b q ha hb` to `SignedTensor.rep`. The operator $\pi_a(A_0)\otimes\pi_b(A_1)$ is `SignedCarrier.hermitianAction a b q ha hb A hA hB`, defined by restricting `TensorRep.action` through the isometric inclusion of the carrier into the raw tensor space. `block A` is `Matrix.blockDiagonal` over `Bool` with `A.1` in the `false` (even) block and `A.2` in the `true` (odd) block, and `TensorRep.action M` is the Kronecker power of `M` acting on functions `τ → Fin q × Bool`.
